<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτοι</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή
			τοι</span></b> , stronger form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή</span>,
		with imper. and subj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τοι δοκεῖτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					436
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1407
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1439
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				544
			</span></i>, etc.; in an oath, c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				765
			</span></i>: in Pl.folld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γε</span>, <i>at
				least not, R.</i><i><span class="en">
				352c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				388b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> after Verbs
			implying negation, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς σ᾽ ἐπεῖχ᾽ ὰεὶ μή τοι . .
					αἰσχύνειν φίλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					518
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
